# SFT execution status v0.93

2026-09-14. The second explicitly approved one-shot read completed, but failed
to extract a standard pytest failed-test summary. It read 99,267 bytes through
two HTTPS GETs, below 4 MiB, using the bound corrected v2 parser. Result remains
`summary_unavailable_or_incomplete`. Failed-test names and the exact remote
failure cause remain unknown. The first and second STOP records and markers
remain intact; no third read occurred and no raw log was saved.

## What the local review establishes

The workflow invokes pytest directly. Its only configured output option is `-q`;
no summary-suppression option or output redirection was found. The active
`ci_source_partition_v1.py` plugin can raise `pytest.UsageError` during startup
before its reporting state exists, or during collection/accounting checks.
Such a failure need not have ordinary FAILED test-node rows. The plugin's own
`SOURCE_SCOPE_ACCOUNTED` JSON is collection accounting, not a passing test result.

A synthetic startup-error example confirms that a summary-only parser rejects
that class of input. This does not prove that startup, collection, OOM, a runtime
error, or any particular test caused the remote failure. The plain-footer
correction remains locally tested, but has not solved the observed extraction
problem. The diagnostic design was too narrow; further speculative footer fixes
or another identical read are not justified.

## Next bounded diagnostic, not yet approved or executed

Use at most two GETs and a 128 KiB log tail to retain only structural format flags,
